# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI buddy — settings template.  Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in ONLY what you have.
#     cp server/.env.example server/.env
#
# THEN START THE GATEWAY WITH `npm start` — not `node gateway.js`. Only the start script passes
# --env-file-if-exists=.env, so a bare `node gateway.js` ignores this file entirely and every key
# below stays invisible (symptom: the picker still shows just the no-key models).
# Everything here is OPTIONAL. With an empty file the buddy still works: it uses the free, no-key
# default endpoint and offers the free models curated in server/model-registry.js (MiMo, Nemotron,
# North Mini Code, Big Pickle, Laguna as of 2026-08-04 — the free list churns; re-check with
#     node server/scripts/verify-models.mjs).
#
# WE SHIP NO KEYS. Every key below is YOURS — a model behind your key bills your account. Add a key
# only if you want its models offered; leave it blank and those options simply never appear in the
# buddy's picker (they are hidden from the menu AND refused by the server, so nothing can 401 in a
# child's face mid-lesson).
#
# After adding anything, confirm it actually answers BEFORE a classroom session:
#     node server/scripts/verify-models.mjs            (spends a real completion — needs your key)
#     node server/scripts/check-openrouter-slugs.mjs   (existence only — NO key needed, safe in CI)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── 1. Providers — set a key to add that provider's models to the buddy's picker ───────────────────
# Each block below is one provider. Set nothing and the buddy still works on the free no-key default.
# Set a provider's key and ALL of its models appear at once. Anything you don't set stays hidden from
# the child's menu AND refused by the server, so nothing they can tap is able to fail with a 401.
#
# An env key here unlocks that provider for EVERYONE this deployment serves. A key pasted in the
# buddy's own picker unlocks it for ONE device only, and never touches the server's disk — that's
# the bring-your-own-key path (README: Bring your own key).

# OpenRouter — one key, many vendors. Adds: Free Router (auto-routes to whichever free model is up),
# GPT (latest), Claude Opus (latest), Gemini 3.5 Flash. Key: https://openrouter.ai
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# DeepSeek, direct. Adds: DeepSeek V4 Flash (fast, low cost), DeepSeek V4 Pro (stronger).
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Alibaba Model Studio (Qwen). Adds: Qwen Plus. BOTH vars are required — Alibaba's URL contains your
# own workspace id and region, so there is no default we can ship. Copy it from the Model Studio
# console; it looks like https://<WorkspaceId>.ap-southeast-1.maas.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1
# (or .cn-beijing. for the Beijing region).
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
ALIBABA_BASE_URL=

# Optional: point a provider at a different endpoint (a proxy, a mirror, a self-hosted gateway).
# Leave blank to use the built-in default for that provider.
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=
ZEN_BASE_URL=


# ── 2. Or point the buddy at ANY OpenAI-compatible provider ───────────────────────────────────────
# The fully flexible path: any provider — or a model on your own hardware — that speaks the OpenAI
# chat-completions shape, including vendors we never listed. Set all three together; the model id then
# appears in the picker as "teacher-configured" even though it is not a built-in option.
#   BUDDY_MODEL_URL   the base URL
#   BUDDY_MODEL_ID    the model to use
#   BUDDY_MODEL_KEY   that provider's key (omit for a local model that needs none)
#
# Verified base URLs for the common cases (read from each vendor's own docs, 2026-07-25):
#   OpenAI           https://api.openai.com/v1                 key: your OpenAI key
#   Run it yourself — nothing leaves the building, no per-message cost, works offline:
#   Ollama           http://localhost:11434/v1                 key: the literal word  ollama
#   LM Studio        http://localhost:1234/v1                  key: any placeholder
# Anthropic and Google do not expose this shape directly — reach those models through OpenRouter above.
BUDDY_MODEL_URL=
BUDDY_MODEL_ID=
BUDDY_MODEL_KEY=

# How much context the model really has, in tokens — powers the buddy's "memory meter".
# Leave blank to use each model's own figure. Set 0 for an honest "unknown" meter instead of a guess.
BUDDY_MODEL_CONTEXT=


# ── 3. Budgets & brakes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Three honestly-separate spend layers — see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-buddy-scope-law-design.md
# §7. Only the middle one lives here; the other two are a browser counter and your provider's own
# console, neither of which this file can set.

# Layer 1 — the child's own guide, enforced in the CHILD'S BROWSER, not here. This is the child's
# per-DAY chat budget: the picker learns it from GET /api/model's `spendCap` and the client's own
# day-keyed localStorage counter refuses new turns once it's spent. A guide, not a security boundary —
# nothing server-side stops a hand-crafted request from ignoring it (that's layers 2 and 3 below).
# The NAME is historical: this is a per-DAY, browser-enforced budget, kept under its old per-lesson
# name so existing deployments' .env files keep working.
# Leave it BLANK for the 120000 tokens/day default. Set 0 to deliberately give the child no budget at
# all (an opt-out, like the brake's 0 below — a garbage value refuses to boot rather than silently
# meaning "unlimited").
BUDDY_MAX_TOKENS_PER_LESSON=

# Layer 2 — the deployment-wide runaway brake (server/brake.js), tokens per UTC day PER INSTANCE.
# Defaults to 2000000. This is abuse protection, not the wallet — it exists so a curl loop or a leaked
# URL hits a bounded daily ceiling instead of your bill; no real child should ever reach it (the
# browser cap above sits ~15x lower). Leave this blank for the default; set 0 to deliberately disable
# it (documented opt-out — the deployer's choice, not an accident: a garbage value refuses to boot
# rather than silently mean "unlimited"). On a serverless/multi-instance deployment the brake is
# per-instance, not global — say so if you rely on it.
BUDDY_DAILY_BRAKE=

# Layer 3 — the wallet, and it is NOT set here. Your REAL spend ceiling is the budget on your own
# provider key — set it in your provider's console. Check that provider's own docs for where; we
# deliberately don't name a console path or feature here for OpenRouter/DeepSeek/Alibaba/etc. — we
# haven't verified those against each vendor's current docs, and a wrong guess is worse than none.

# Which buddy actions are allowed, comma-separated. Blank = all of them.
# Choices: setParam, createGroup, addItems, removeItems, runCheck, undoLast, rememberUser
BUDDY_ENABLED_OPS=


# ── 4. Server ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port the gateway listens on (default 8787).
BUDDY_PORT=

# Interface to bind (default 127.0.0.1 — loopback-only, safe for a laptop: this process holds the
# model credential and serves server source via a few read-only mounts, so binding every interface
# would expose it to the whole LAN/network by default). A real deployment sitting behind a platform
# proxy (Render, Fly, a school's own reverse proxy, etc.) sets 0.0.0.0 deliberately, once you know the
# proxy — not the open internet — is what's actually reachable.
BUDDY_HOST=

# Where the buddy's baked default persona/notes seeds are read from at boot (default: server/memory).
# The gateway NEVER writes here — a child's own memory travels in their champion file, not on disk.
BUDDY_MEMORY_DIR=
